Set the NanoPi R2C RTL8153 RJ45 LED mode.
The value comes from OpenWrt's R2S devicetree support:
https://lists.openwrt.org/pipermail/openwrt-devel/2021-February/033822.html

Applied to rk3328-nanopi-r2c.dts: the r2c dtb includes the shared
rk3328-nanopi-r2.dtsi (via rk3328-nanopi-r2c.dtsi), where the rtl8153
node label is defined, so the &rtl8153 overlay reference resolves here.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2c.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2c.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2c.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2c.dts
@@ -14,3 +14,7 @@
 	model = "FriendlyElec NanoPi R2C";
 	compatible = "friendlyarm,nanopi-r2c", "rockchip,rk3328";
 };
+
+&rtl8153 {
+	realtek,led-data = <0x87>;
+};
